WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.396
Step 1. Open the schedule. When an appointment is booked on a template,

1.2
00:00:05.396 --> 00:00:08.730
Care uses its charges to create a charge item.

1.3
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:14.014
Select Users, See Details for the practitioner, then Availability.

2.1
00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:17.241
Step 2. Open the charges of the template.

2.2
00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:20.436
On the template card, select Manage Charges.

2.3
00:00:20.436 --> 00:00:23.849
The Select Charge Item Definitions sheet opens,

2.4
00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:28.342
with the text Select or Create Charge Item Definitions.

3.1
00:00:28.342 --> 00:00:31.469
Step 3. Choose the consultation charge.

3.2
00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:36.705
In Consultation Charge, search for and select a charge item definition.

3.3
00:00:36.705 --> 00:00:43.031
This field is required. If it is missing, select Create Charge Item Definition.

4.1
00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:47.966
Step 4. Set the re-visit rule. Enter the Re-visit allowed days.

4.2
00:00:47.966 --> 00:00:54.139
A return visit within these days gets the re-visit charge; if no re-visit charge is

4.3
00:00:54.139 --> 00:00:56.721
set, Care creates no charge.

5.1
00:00:56.721 --> 00:00:58.813
Step 5. Save the charges.

5.2
00:00:58.813 --> 00:01:04.042
Select Save, which is available after you choose a consultation charge.

5.3
00:01:04.042 --> 00:01:08.593
Care shows Charge item definition updated successfully.
